    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Does this difficulty with staying focused happen in other areas of your life as well, such as at work or when you are trying to complete tasks on your own?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S002",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, it definitely happens when I'm doing things on my own, too. Like... if I sit down to work out a catering order, or if I'm listening through a parish planning call. We do this big community dinner thing at the church, and lately they've been wanting to add more vegetarian options, which I get, but nobody actually eats the baked eggplant dish they insist on making. It just sits there getting cold in those metal chafing dishes. Those little gel fuel cans they put underneath them always smell so terrible, don't they? It always reminds me of being in a chemistry lab back in college, just that harsh chemical smell. \n\nBut, um... right, the tasks. When I'm doing that stuff, I start off fine. I'm sitting there, ready to go. But before long, my mind just wanders off completely. I'll look down at the page and realize I have to go back over the exact same notes like I never even read them in the first place.",
