      "doctor_question": "Aside from the difficulty with focus, have you often felt like you are 'driven by a motor' or found it hard to sit still for long periods of time?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, not really. I'm actually pretty content just sitting. My wife is the one who can't sit still, honestly. She's always up and doing something, wiping down the counters, rearranging the throw pillows... we have these green velvet pillows on the couch, and she insists they have to be placed exactly right or the whole room looks off. She got them at this little boutique downtown that went out of business last year. It's a shame, too, because they had the best scented candles. This one called \"Fireside Ember\" or something like that, it smelled just like a real wood-burning fireplace. We used to have a real fireplace in our first house, but it was so drafty in the winter. You'd sit near it and freeze unless a fire was actually going. But no, I don't feel like I have a motor running or anything. I can sit in my recliner for hours just fine.",
