    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever been told by others, or do you feel yourself, that you have a tendency to act or speak impulsively without thinking through the consequences first?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, I don't think so. I'm usually pretty careful about what I say. Well, most of the time. My brother, on the other hand, he'll just blurt out whatever comes to his mind. He did that at our cousin's wedding a few years ago. We were all at the reception, and they had this massive ice sculpture of a swan right in the middle of the buffet table. It was huge, took up half the space where the shrimp cocktail was supposed to go. I don't even know how they got it in there without it melting, because it was mid-July and the air conditioning in that hall was struggling. You could see condensation dripping down the walls. Anyway, he made some comment about the bride's dress right to her face, something about it looking like a meringue pie. She didn't talk to him for a year after that. But me? No, I usually think before I speak. I'm not really one to just jump into things or talk without thinking.",
